# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents (and humans) working in **{{.Name}}**. {{.Description}}

## Ground rules

- Read this file first. Every command below is non-interactive and safe to run.
- Do not push to `main`. Work on a branch `type/short-desc`, open a pull request. The PR title is a Conventional Commits subject (`feat(api): add health route`).
{{- if .OpenSource}}
- Every commit needs a `Signed-off-by` trailer (`git commit -s`); see CONTRIBUTING.md.
{{- end}}
- Tests come first: for a bug, write the failing regression test, then fix it.
- Versions are pinned. Do not use `latest`; bump a version deliberately and say why.
- Run the project's own checks before you report done (see the sections below).

## Dev environment

`atlas dev` starts every service from `atlas.yaml` (https://atlas.codeatlas.com.br). Agents can use the atlas MCP
server (`atlas mcp`) to read status and logs and restart services. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` first.

## Layout

This repository was generated by [vkd](https://github.com/vkdprojects/vkd) from the blueprints recorded in
`.vkd/answers.yaml` ({{join ", " .Components}}). `vkd update` re-renders and three-way merges, so keep edits
to generated files small and intentional. `vkd add <blueprint>` adds a component.
